-- title:
--   Kneser reduction: strong approximation away from v in double-coset form
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ with $a<0$ and $b<0$, so that $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is definite, and let $O\subseteq\mathbb H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an order in the sense of the project: $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $\mathbb H$, and it is finitely generated. Fix a prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$. Throughout, for a prime $w$, reduced norms on $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ are read through any ring isomorphism $\varphi$ onto $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ coordinatewise, with $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-bx_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+abx_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$, and $\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w$ denotes the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_w$. The first hypothesis asks: for every prime $w\neq v$ such that $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ has a nonzero non-unit, for every $s'$ in that algebra of reduced norm $1$ in the above sense, and for every nonzero $M\in\mathbb N$, there is $\beta\in\mathbb H$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$ such that $\beta\otimes 1=1+M\cdot z$ with $z\in\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w'$ for every prime $w'\notin\{v,w\}$, and $\beta\otimes 1=s'+M\cdot z$ with $z\in\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w$. Let $y$ be a unit of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ whose component at each prime $w\neq v$, obtained by evaluating the finite adele factor at $w$, has reduced norm $1$ in the above sense. The conclusion: there are a unit $\beta$ of $\mathbb H$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ such that $u$ stabilises, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in O$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele, the component of $g$ at every prime $w\neq v$ equals $1$, and $y=\iota(\beta)\,g\,u$, where $\iota$ is the map on unit groups induced by $\mathbb H\hookrightarrow\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$.
--
--   This is Kneser's reduction of strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite rational quaternion algebra, with respect to the set of places $\{\infty,v\}$ and in double-coset form: an approximation hypothesis concerning single split local factors away from $v$ yields the factorisation $y\in\mathbb H^{\times}\cdot\mathbb H_v^{\times}\cdot\widehat O^{\times}$. It is used to obtain the unconditional form of the statement, in which the local hypothesis is replaced by the requirement that all components away from $v$ have reduced norm $1$.
